@startuml
title ioScope Process View
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Qt UI Thread" {
  component "ioQtScopeWindow" as qtWindow
  component "ioCompactOscilloscopeView" as compactView
  component "ioDetailedOscilloscopeView" as detailedView
  component "ioOscilloscopeController" as controller
  component "ioOscilloscopeModel" as model
  component "ioLiveOscilloscopeSession" as liveSession
  component "ioPipelineController" as pipelineController
  component "ioFilterPipeline" as filterPipeline
  component "ioWaveformGenerator" as generator
}

rectangle "FTDI Read Thread" {
  component "ioUsbReadController" as readWorker
  component "ioReadableByteStream" as readable
}

rectangle "FTDI Write Thread" {
  component "ioUsbWriteController" as writeWorker
  component "ioWritableByteStream" as writable
}

queue "ioDataBuffer\nCircular Buffer" as buffer

qtWindow --> controller : view selection / input source
controller --> model : update control state
model --> generator : acquire raw samples
model --> filterPipeline : scale + offset pipeline
controller --> liveSession : start / stop / refresh live mode
liveSession --> pipelineController : configure background transfer
controller --> compactView : render(state)
controller --> detailedView : render(state)

readWorker --> readable : read_bytes()
readWorker --> buffer : push(bytes)
writeWorker --> buffer : pop(bytes)
writeWorker --> writable : write_bytes()

note right of buffer
Required concurrent handoff:
one read thread and one write thread
share the bounded circular buffer.
end note

note left of controller
controller, model, waveform generation,
filtering, live-session coordination,
and rendering all run on the
Qt UI thread.
end note

note right of qtWindow
The window hosts both concrete Qt view instances.
It selects visibility but does not act as a
second MVC View abstraction.
end note

@enduml
